<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Multi-Level Carriers:</strong> Multilevel carriers are commonly used for transporting multiple vehicles simultaneously, allowing for efficient use of space. These carriers have tiers, enabling them to transport vehicles of varying sizes.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Tandem Axle Carriers:</strong> Tandem axle carriers provide more space for larger vehicles, ensuring they can accommodate both cars and trucks effectively.</span></li>
